{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":22085996,"ns":0,"title":"Creighton's slender opossum","revisions":[{"revid":1382801589,"parentid":1382801585,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:55:35Z","size":1866,"sha1":"0d8392f642fb68c0fbc20507d26ca709781518af","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Species of marsupial}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| name = Creighton's slender opossum\n| image =\n| status = DD\n| status_system = IUCN3.1\n| status_ref = <ref name=\"iucn status 19 November 2021\">{{cite iucn |author=Tarifa, T. |date=2016 |title=''Marmosops creightoni'' |volume=2016 |article-number=e.T136803A22178229 |doi=10.2305/IUCN.UK.2016-1.RLTS.T136803A22178229.en |access-date=19 November 2021}}</ref>\n| genus = Marmosops\n| species = creightoni\n| authority = [[Robert S. Voss|Voss]], Tarifa & Yensen, 2004\n| synonyms = \n| range_map = Marmosops creightoni area.png\n| range_map_caption = Creighton's slender opossum range\n}}\n\n'''Creighton's slender opossum''' ('''''Marmosops creightoni'''''), also known commonly as '''Voss' slender opossum'''<ref name = \"Beolens\"/> is a species of [[South America]]n [[opossum]] of the family [[Didelphidae]]. It is known only from the valley of the [[Rio Zongo]] in [[La Paz Department, Bolivia]], where it lives in [[Andes|Andean]] [[cloud forest]]s at elevations between 1800 and 3000 m.<ref name=\"iucn status 19 November 2021\" /> It was named after [[G. Ken Creighton]] by fellow American zoologist [[Robert S. Voss]].<ref name = \"Beolens\">{{Cite book\n  | last = Beolens | first = Bo |author2=Watkins, Michael |author3=Grayson, Michael\n  | title = The Eponym Dictionary of Mammals\n  | publisher = [[The Johns Hopkins University Press]]\n  | date = 2009-09-28 | location = [[Baltimore]] | page =90\n  | url = http://google.com/books?id=I-kSmWLc6vYC&pg=PA90\n  | isbn = 978-0-8018-9304-9| oclc = 270129903}}</ref>\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Didelphimorphia|D.}}\n{{